   "head": null,
   "text": "This article extended our study of LLM-based monolith decomposition from a single-shot pipeline to an agentic workflow, in which LLM agents construct evidence, infer provisional domain knowledge, and propose alternative candidates, while deterministic agents repair, validate, select, and refine the result without access to any reference. We compared the workflow with single-shot prompting and an autonomous coding agent under matched conditions, across four LLMs and four benchmark systems.",
